@startuml Timing_AuthenticationFlow
!theme plain
title Authentication Process - Timing Diagram

robust "Browser" as Browser
robust "Frontend" as Frontend
robust "Backend" as Backend
robust "Database" as Database

@Browser
0 is Idle
50 is ClickLogin
100 is FormFilled
150 is Submitting
200 is Waiting
300 is Redirecting
350 is DashboardLoaded

@Frontend
0 is Idle
100 is FormDisplay
150 is ValidateInput
200 is SendRequest
250 is Processing
300 is ReceiveResponse
320 is StoreToken
350 is RouteChange

@Backend
0 is Idle
200 is ReceiveRequest
220 is QueryDB
260 is VerifyPassword
280 is GenerateJWT
300 is SendResponse

@Database
0 is Idle
220 is ExecuteQuery
240 is ReturnData

Browser -> Frontend @ 100 : User clicks login
Frontend -> Frontend @ 150 : Validate form
Frontend -> Backend @ 200 : POST /api/login
Backend -> Database @ 220 : SELECT user
Database -> Backend @ 240 : User data
Backend -> Backend @ 260 : Verify password
Backend -> Backend @ 280 : Generate token
Backend -> Frontend @ 300 : {token, user}
Frontend -> Frontend @ 320 : Store token
Frontend -> Browser @ 350 : Redirect to dashboard

@enduml

